    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-lūcesco</span></b> , luxi,
			lucescĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> [re-luceo], <i>to
				grow bright again</i>, <i>to shine out</i>, <i>become clear</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luna plena luminis effigie relucescit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 8, § 870</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solis imago reluxit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 769</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reluxit dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					4, 81 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—<i>Impers.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paulum reluxit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 6, 20, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
